{"title":"2004 USAMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Titu Andreescu</i>)\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be positive real numbers.  Prove that\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/7/79771fe63edbd1f0a6851321552b4a1c8d6f9bf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^5 - a^2 + 3)(b^5 - b^2 + 3)(c^5 - c^2 + 3) \\ge (a+b+c)^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"412\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/jmXSmmfO7pQ?si=dxJ6At7KHlcn2NT5\">https://youtu.be/jmXSmmfO7pQ?si=dxJ6At7KHlcn2NT5</a> [Video Solution by little fermat]\n</p><p>We first note that for positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/3/5336b8c707a4a71dc4a872c4ef4ffa08698eac2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^5 + 1 \\ge x^3 + x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"17\" />.  We may prove this in the following ways:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/48524d3889ec8433cb03669176e738011df245b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> must be both lesser than, both equal to, or both greater than 1, by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rearrangement_inequality\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Rearrangement inequality\">rearrangement inequality</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/3/be3def09a651775cfaf14dc4fc6febb69e350a65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 \\cdot x^3 + 1 \\cdot 1 \\ge x^2 \\cdot 1 + 1 \\cdot x^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"227\" height=\"17\" />.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/0/8506cdfc2f65bfb3e57e2e74ad11cde48c0ff863.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/600d31c33edfd279cf4d56cd93d85f449d8a0f5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" /> have the same sign, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/b/bcbbd97ce7b526340c4594ae6c83796090cfecf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le (x^2 - 1)(x^3 - 1) = x^5 - x^3 - x^2 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"312\" height=\"19\" />, with equality when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>By weighted <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AM-GM\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AM-GM\">AM-GM</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f6497bedb87068782dbd6060a1b0a5693c9dc4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5}x^5 + \\frac{3}{5} \\ge x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"107\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e777e6c822fef3921b162fde22018b6a2795142f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{5}x^5 + \\frac{2}{5} \\ge x^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"107\" height=\"37\" />.  Adding these gives the desired inequality.  Equivalently, the desired inequality is a case of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Muirhead%27s_Inequality\" title=\"Muirhead&#39;s Inequality\">Muirhead's Inequality</a>.</li></ul>\n<p>It thus becomes sufficient to prove that\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/0/62098ad17d1a295369975da15e1859bdb48043df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a^3 + 2)(b^3 + 2)(c^3 + 2) \\ge (a+b+c)^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"298\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>We present two proofs of this inequality:\n</p>\n<ul><li>By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=H%C3%B6lder%27s_Inequality\" title=\"Hölder&#39;s Inequality\">Hölder's Inequality</a>,</li></ul>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/4/a64ff37f71a73cb3ac767a5bee4fd91052d97382.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{matrix}(m_{1,1} + m_{1,2} + m_{1,3})(m_{2,1} + m_{2,2} + m_{2,3})(m_{3,1} + m_{3,2} + m_{3,3}) \\ge \\\\ \\qquad \\qquad \\qquad\\left[ (m_{1,1}m_{2,1}m_{3,1})^{1/3} + (m_{2,1}m_{2,2}m_{2,3})^{1/3} + (m_{3,1}m_{3,2}m_{3,3})^{1/3} \\right] ^3.\\end{matrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"587\" height=\"47\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>We get the desired inequality by taking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/3/9d33c7fd0edf66b9fffd34e4a199ed181b2c6648.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{1,1} = a^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/0/860b1f81148e31305f17c469602cf0c5724e56ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{2,2} = b^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/879cf7def2aabc7478bb37b7b080f7ec27201f80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{3,3} = c^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"19\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/0/1100bbad87911265e7b3ac89a1a51981e0c86953.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{x,y} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"16\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/d/74ddb8309acb92903e40f1ba96475de8f7761cdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\neq y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" />. We have equality if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/f/8dfa0e69992284ec2f621b4c356a3edbf99c9f76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = b = c = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"106\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/d/f7dbac5105c1f55e9ecb7d9184f7365882effa98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\sqrt{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/f/fcfc3e170e93d8d56e51cec015e9bf1e847c7307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\sqrt{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"21\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/7/6173e5737bd69c3c938d816ad279d39669dae310.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = \\sqrt{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />. Then some two of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are both at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or both at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Without loss of generality, say these are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Then the sequences <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/f/08fd695f81176db3e8659f86d8602466deaabd66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, 1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/2/6d2945aadcf60e63031f9d2489495448aa7079c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 1, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> are oppositely sorted, yielding</li></ul>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/9/0495feadff61baff8e3a6c73063702d1402be01b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^6 + 1 + 1)(1 + 1 + y^6) \\ge 3(x^6 + 1 + y^6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"322\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chebyshev%27s_Inequality\" title=\"Chebyshev&#39;s Inequality\">Chebyshev's Inequality</a>. By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cauchy-Schwarz_Inequality\" title=\"Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality\">Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality</a> we have\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/a/7da38a2f3e22088cebc1061732a0df2954594ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^6 + 1 + y^6)(1 + z^6 + 1) \\ge (x^3 + y^3 + z^3)^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"341\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Applying Chebyshev's and the Cauchy-Schwarz Inequalities each once more, we get\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39c742105a4118d858f9391449c9b583a5959700.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(x^3 + y^3 + z^3) \\ge (x^2 + y^2 + z^2)(x+y+z),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"345\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>and\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/b/49b431b5ddd9ede6113060fdf5164b69b2bb3d8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^3 + y^3 + z^3)(x+y+z) \\ge (x^2 + y^2 + z^2)^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"343\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Multiplying the above four inequalities together yields\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/9/cc9ba59b82f1b1da058d09a0b6fe0cddc43a22d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^6 + 2)(y^6 + 2)(z^6 + 2) \\ge (x^2 + y^2 + z^2)^3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"334\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>as desired, with equality if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/9/0f99894c74d93974e12480aa9d209c7e86df18cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = y = z = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<ul><li>First, expand the left side of the inequality to get</li></ul>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/9/02904e4e5b43f8529061bb5d52a8a79885ee6bff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3b^3c^3 + 4(a^3 + b^3 + c^3) + 2(a^3b^3 + a^3c^3 + b^3c^3) + 8.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"409\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>By the AM-GM inequality, it is true that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/b/59b5d98a96ea9fd456f0072736e0f68fdf81ae1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3 + a^3b^3 + 1 \\ge 3a^2b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"163\" height=\"19\" />, and so it is clear that\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/a/60a184dc3220fefaa94c27f9dbb128218e521e08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3b^3c^3 + 4(a^3 + b^3 + c^3) + 2(a^3b^3 + a^3c^3 + b^3c^3) + 8 \\ge a^3b^3c^3 + 2(a^3 + b^3 + c^3) + 2 + 3a^2b + 3ab^2 + 3bc^2 + 3b^2c + 3c^2a + 3ca^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"983\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Additionally, again by AM-GM, it is true that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accd76b40c6f132cf1222904fa37666d79a9c0fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3b^3c^3 + a^3 + b^3 + c^3 + 1 + 1 \\ge 6abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"285\" height=\"19\" />, and so\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/e/e5e4f5021de463e3f2c1d9f1e332d1b7dc3ad631.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3b^3c^3 + 2(a^3 + b^3 + c^3) + 2 + 3a^2b + 3ab^2 + 3bc^2 + 3b^2c + 3c^2a + 3ca^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"552\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f54b3a1e339935452026f045307a71c82d28408.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ge a^3 + b^3 + c^3 + 3a^2b + 3ab^2 + 3bc^2 + 3b^2c + 3c^2a + 3ca^2 + 6abc = {(a + b + c)}^3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"624\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n</center> \n<p>as desired.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><i>It is also possible to solve this inequality by expanding terms and applying brute force, either before or after proving that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/b/39b3a6d6cd9ffa3ca0587ee7ab5d2c87c3344e64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^5 - x^2 + 3 \\ge x^3 + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"162\" height=\"17\" />.</i>\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2004_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_USAMO\" title=\"2004 USAMO\">2004 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2004 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2004\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2004 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017002258\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.048 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.067 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 296/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1663/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9582/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   19.299      1 -total\n 39.09%    7.543      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 29.86%    5.762      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n 29.32%    5.658      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4793:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017002258 and revision id 228079. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}